# The sandbox the Flatpak runs in: what `flatpak build-finish` writes into the
# application's metadata (packaging/build-client-flatpak.sh), one argument a
# line. Each is a thing the client does; nothing here is for convenience.
#
# A window: Wayland, and X11 where the session has no Wayland, with the shared
# memory X11 uses, and the GPU SDL renders on.
--socket=wayland
--socket=fallback-x11
--share=ipc
--device=dri
# The workspace's server, and the calls' relay.
--share=network
# The microphone, the speakers, and the camera and screen streams the portals
# hand over (client/core/media/cap_portal.c), all on PipeWire.
--filesystem=xdg-run/pipewire-0
# On the session bus: the portals (screen and camera capture, the desktop's
# settings, file pickers), which every Flatpak reaches; desktop notifications
# (client/shared/osnotify_linux.c); the tray's StatusNotifierItem host; the
# accessibility bus (client/gui/platform/linux/a11y_atspi.c); and the desktop's
# Secret Service, where libsecret keeps the session (client/shared/
# secret_libsecret.c), which the client asks directly as the .deb's does, so
# libsecret is told to use it rather than its file in the sandbox.
--talk-name=org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop
--talk-name=org.freedesktop.Notifications
--talk-name=org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher
--talk-name=org.a11y.Bus
--talk-name=org.freedesktop.secrets
--env=SECRET_BACKEND=service
